Overfull \hbox (2290.49234pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 7621--7621
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Solution: Consider the following graph formulation. Treat eac
h pixel in the image as a vertex in the graph, with an edge between two neighbo
ring pixels. The weight of this edge should be proportional to how dark the pix
els are. A segmentation between two lines is a path in this graph from the left
 to right side of the page. We seek a relatively straight path that avoids as m
uch blackness as possible. This suggests that the shortest path in the pixel gr
aph will likely find a good line segmentation.[] 
