Overfull \hbox (2563.49155pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 7640--7640
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Although a breadth-first search could also be used to enumera
te solutions, a depth-first search is greatly preferred because it uses much le
ss space. The current state of a search is completely represented by the path f
rom the root to the current depth-first search node. This requires space propor
tional to the height of the tree. In breadth-first search, the queue stores all
 the nodes at the current level, which is proportional to the width of the sear
ch tree. For most interesting problems, the width of the tree grows exponential
ly with its height.[] 
 []


