ch properties make a particular problem hard. This can provide direction to mod
el it in different ways, or exploit more benevolent characteristics of the prob
lem. Developing a sense for which problems are hard is an important skill for a
lgorithm designers, and only comes from hands-on experience with proving hardne
ss.[] 
 []


