f matrix inversion, since $A x=B \leftrightarrow A^{-1} A x=A^{-1} B$, where $I
=A^{-1} A$ is the identity matrix. Avoid it, however, because matrix inversion 
proves to be three times slower than Gaussian elimination. LU-decomposition is 
very useful to invert matrices as well as compute determinants (see Section 16.
4 (page 475).[] 
