m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s rule for fast polynomial evaluation. When $P(x)=\sum_
{i=0}^{n} c_{i} \cdot x^{i}$ is blindly evaluated term by term, $O\left(n^{2}\r
ight)$ multiplications will be performed. Much better is observing that $P(x)=c
_{0}+$ $x\left(c_{1}+x\left(c_{2}+x\left(c_{3}+\ldots\right)\right)\right.$ ), 
