items, and let $C\left[i, S^{\prime}\right]$ be true if and only if there is a 
subset of $S^{\prime}$ whose size adds up exactly to $i$. Thus, $C[i, \emptyset
]$ is false for all $1 \leq i \leq C$. One by one we add a new item $s_{j}$ to 
$S^{\prime}$ and update the affected values of $C\left[i, S^{\prime}\right]$. O
bserve that[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (631.49716pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 C\left[i, S^{\prime} \cup s_{j}\right]=\text { true iff }\lef
t(C\left[i, S^{\prime}\right]=\text { true }\right) \text { or }\left(C\left[i-
s_{j}, S^{\prime}\right]=\text { true }\right)[] 
 []


