say eliminating undesirable high- and/or low-frequency components. Taking an in
verse Fourier transform then gets us back into the time domain. For example, th
e sharp spike in the plot above represents the period of the single sine functi
on that closely models the input data. The rest is noise.[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (1203.7455pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Image compression - A smoothed, filtered image contains les
s information than the original, while retaining a similar appearance. By elimi
nating the coefficients of sine functions that contribute relatively little to 
the image, we reduce the size of the image at little cost in image fidelity.[] 

 []


