Overfull \hbox (227.24834pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 & \text { for } i=1 \text { to } n-1 \text { do } \operatorna
me{swap}[a[i], a[\operatorname{Random}[1, n]]] ;[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (1980.74324pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Such subtleties demonstrate why you must be very careful with
 random generation algorithms. Indeed, I recommend that you perform reasonably 
extensive experiments with any random generator before trusting it. For example
, generate 10,000 random permutations of length 4 and verify that all 24 distin
ct permutations occur approximately the same number of times. If you know how t
o test for statistical significance, you are in even better shape.[] 
