[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Discussion: Devising the best schedule to satisfy a set of co
nstraints is fundamental to many applications. Mapping tasks to processors is a
 critical aspect of any parallel-processing system. Poor scheduling can leave m
any machines sitting idle while one bottleneck task is performed. Assigning peo
ple-to-jobs, meetings-to-rooms, or courses-to-exam periods are all scheduling p
roblems.[] 
 []


