[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Scheduling problems differ widely in the nature of the constr
aints that must be satisfied and the type of schedule desired. Several other ca
talog problems have connections to variants of scheduling:[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (274.4982pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Topological sort constructs a schedule consistent with prec
edence constraints in a DAG. See Section 18.2 (page 546).[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (216.74837pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 - Bipartite matching assigns jobs to workers with appropriate
 skills for them. See Section 18.6 (page 562 .[] 
 []


