8.1 (page 244), Prim\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s algorithm runs in $O\le
ft(n^{2}\right)$, while Kruskal\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s algorithm ta
kes $O(m \log m)$ time. Prim\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s algorithm is th
us faster on dense graphs, while Kruskal\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s is 
faster on sparse graphs. That said, Prim\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s alg
orithm can be implemented in $O(m+n \lg n)$ time using more advanced data struc
tures, so a Prim\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s implementation using pairin
g heaps would be the fastest practical choice for both sparse and dense graphs.
[] 
