[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 The best theoretical bounds on finding minimum spanning trees
 tell a complicated story. Karger, Klein, and Tarjan KKT95 give a linear-time r
andomized algorithm for MSTs, based again on Borukva\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/
m/n/10 s algorithm. Chazelle Cha00 give a deterministic $O(n \alpha(m, n))$ alg
orithm, where $\alpha(m, n)$ is the inverse Ackerman function. Pettie and Ramac
handran PR02 give a provably optimal algorithm whose exact running time is (par
