Overfull \hbox (1928.2434pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 A spanner $S(G)$ of a given graph $G$ is a subgraph that offe
rs an effective compromise between two competing network objectives. To be prec
ise, $S(G)$ must have total weight close to the MST of $G$ while guaranteeing t
hat the shortest path between vertices $x$ and $y$ in $S(G)$ approaches the sho
rtest path in the full graph $G$. The monograph of Narasimhan and Smid NS07 pro
vides a complete, up-to-date survey on spanner networks.[] 
 []


