into regions containing distinct objects. Region boundaries can be thought of a
s paths over the image that avoid cutting through object pixels as much as poss
ible. This grid of pixels can be modeled as a graph, with the cost of an edge r
eflecting the color transitions between neighboring pixels. The shortest path i
n such a weighted graph defines a promising potential boundary between two regi
ons.[] 
