he even-numbered edges of $P$ from $M$ with the odd-numbered edges of $P$. Berg
e\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s theorem states that a matching is maximum 
iff it does not contain any augmenting path. Therefore, we can construct maximu
m-cardinality matchings by searching for augmenting paths, and stop when none e
xist.[] 
