Overfull \hbox (2101.49289pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 The most natural tree-drawing algorithms assume rooted trees.
 However, they can be used equally well with free trees, after selecting one ve
rtex to serve as the root of the drawing. This faux-root can be selected arbitr
arily, or, even better, by using a center vertex of the tree. A center vertex m
inimizes the maximum distance to other vertices. This tree center can be identi
fied in linear time, by repeatedly trimming all the leaves until only the cente
r remains.[] 
