r page, and then partition the page into the root-degree number of top-down str
ips. Deleting the root creates a set of subtrees, each of which is assigned to 
its own strip. Draw each subtree recursively, by placing its new root (the vert
ex adjacent to the old root) in the center of its strip a fixed distance down f
rom the top, with a line from old root to new root. The output figure above is 
a nice ranked embedding of a balanced binary tree.[] 
