ntains greedy and 2-approximate heuristics for vertex cover.[] 
 []


Overfull \hbox (2085.74294pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Notes: Karp Kar72 first proved that vertex-cover is NP-comple
te. A diverse set of heuristics yield 2 -approximation algorithms for vertex co
ver, including randomized rounding. Good expositions on these 2-approximation a
lgorithms include CLRS09] Pas97, Vaz04, WS11. The example that the greedy algor
ithm can be as bad as $\lg n$ times optimal is due to Joh74 and presented in PS
98. Experimental studies of vertex cover heuristics include ACL12, GMPV06, GW97
