Overfull \hbox (2253.74245pt too wide) in paragraph at lines 18033--18033
[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 The Christofides heuristic Chr76 is an improvement over the m
inimum spanning tree heuristic and guarantees a tour whose cost is at most $3 /
 2$ times optimal on Euclidean graphs. It runs in $O\left(n^{3}\right)$, where 
the bottleneck is the time it takes to find a minimum-weight perfect matching (
see Section 18.6 (page 562). An exciting recent result yields a constant-factor
 approximation for the more general case of asymmetric TSP STV17. The minimum s
panning tree heuristic is due to RSL77.[] 
