determining the automorphism group of a vertex-colored graph. Nauty also produc
es a canonical labeling of the graph, to assist in isomorphism testing. It can 
test most graphs with fewer than a hundred vertices in well under a second. Nau
ty is available at http://pallini.di.uniroma1.it/. The theory behind nauty and 
an affiliate program Traces are described in McK81, MP14].[] 
