=\left(x^{\prime}, y^{\prime}\right)$ in the plane? We can project the sampled 
points on the plane, and then triangulate them. This triangulation partitions t
he plane into triangles, so we can estimate height by interpolating between the
 heights ( $z$-coordinates) of the three points of the triangle that contain $q
$. Furthermore, this triangulation and the associated height values define a mo
untain surface suitable for graphics rendering.[] 
