h internal edge of any triangulation is shared between two triangles. The four 
vertices defining these two triangles form either (a) a convex quadrilateral, o
r (b) a triangle with a triangular bite taken out of it. The beauty of the conv
ex case is that exchanging the internal edge with a chord linking the other two
