query point $q$ - a cell whose boundary points are good candidates to be close 
neighbors. Now suppose we search for a point $q^{\prime}$, which is a small ran
dom perturbation of $q$. It should land in a different but nearby cell, one of 
whose boundary points might prove to be an even closer neighbor of $q$. Repeati
