[]\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 Kirkpatrick\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 s elegant triang
le refinement method Kir83] builds a hierarchy of triangulations above the actu
al planar subdivision, such that each triangle on a given level intersects only
 a constant number of triangles on the following level. Each triangulation is a
 fraction of the size of the subsequent one, so the total space is linear by su
mming up a geometric series. Furthermore, the height of the hierarchy is $O(\lg
 n)$, ensuring fast query times. An alternative algorithm realizing the same ti
me bounds is EGS86. The slab method described above is due to DL76 and is prese
nted in PS85. Expositions on the inside-outside test for simple polygons includ
e O\TS1/lmtt/m/n/10 '\T1/lmtt/m/n/10 R01 PS85 SR03.[] 
